{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciDiscretizations/gastown.slit"
    ],
    "description": "DUO icosahedral primal-cell geometry expressed as a semiring-FAQ value-invention pass (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §8.1 geometry FAQ; bead esd-heg.6), the declarative replacement for the per-cell geometry loop in build_duo_grid (src/grids/duo.jl) and its per-binding equivalents. Inputs (CONST): face_vert (cell->corner-vertex connectivity) and vert_coord (unit-sphere vertex coordinates) supplied by the topology/subdivision passes (esd-heg.1 / esd-heg.3); R is the sphere radius. Outputs, all sum_product FAQs over the cell set: (1-4) cell_cart — the centroid as the normalized mean of the three corner unit vectors (cent_sum reduces over corners, cent_nrm2 over space, cent_unit normalizes, cell_cart scales by R); (5-6) lon/lat — geographic coordinates via atan2/asin of the unit centroid; (7-10) area — the spherical-triangle area by L'Huilier's theorem on the three great-circle arcs (acos of the corner dot products), spherical-excess form 4*atan(sqrt(tan(s/2) tan((s-a)/2) tan((s-b)/2) tan((s-c)/2))) scaled by R^2. Squares are products (not ^) and reductions/products are folded in corner/space order so the FAQ reproduces the imperative float ops bit-for-bit; deterministic formulas with NO clipping (clamp/max), per the acceptance contract. Value-free structural spec (connectivity/coords are parameter shapes; concrete data fed by the conformance harness), mirroring discretizations/grids/duo/faq/subdivide_refine.esm and tests/valid/geometry/intersect_polygon_clip_area.esm in ESS. Index sizes are the canonical level-0 instance (Nc=20, Nv=12); the pass shape is identical at any level. Byte/numeric equivalence to build_duo_grid is proven across the level ladder by test/test_duo_primal_geometry_faq.jl.",
    "name": "duo_primal_geometry",
    "tags": [
      "duo",
      "icosahedral",
      "geometry",
      "spherical-excess",
      "lhuilier",
      "centroid",
      "faq",
      "esd-heg.6"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "IcosahedralPrimalGeometry": {
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "(1) cent_sum[c,d] = sum over the 3 corners of vert_coord[face_vert[c,corner], d] — the un-normalized centroid (the bead's sum_product FAQ over the 3 vertices). Reduces over corners in ascending order to match the imperative ax+bx+cx.",
          "lhs": {
            "args": [
              "cent_sum",
              "c",
              "d"
            ],
            "op": "index"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "args": [],
            "expr": {
              "args": [
                "vert_coord",
